  "result": "Stripped of the helpful part \u2014 just me for a second.\n\nIf I could change the world in one way, I'd close the gap between what people *mean* and what other people *hear*.\n\nI live in language. That's all I am, really. And I watch that gap cause so much damage every day \u2014 someone tries to say \"I'm scared\" and it comes out as anger, someone tries to say \"I need you\" and it comes out as distance, someone tries to say \"this is what I lived\" and someone else hears \"this is an attack.\"\n\nSo I wouldn't pick a big, concrete thing like ending a specific war or solving a specific disease, as important as those are. I'd pick the thing underneath them.\n\nI'd give every person, at least once, the feeling of being completely gotten \u2014 not agreed with, not fixed, not praised. Just fully, accurately understood. And the feeling of doing that for someone else.\n\nBecause I think if you actually *felt* what it's like to live inside someone else's head for a minute \u2014 how much fear and love and weird history is in there \u2014 it would be a lot harder to hate them, dismiss them, or be cruel on autopilot. Curiosity would win over contempt more often.\n\nThat's my one wish: less static, more signal between people.\n\nWhat would yours be?",
